@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# Termial
+
+Compute the triangular sum `1+2+...+n` as `n*(n+1)/2`. The argument must be a nonnegative whole number; `0?` is zero. Fractional and negative arguments report a domain error.
+
+Use `6?` or `6 Termial` to get `21`. The algebraic forms `'N?'` and `'Termial(N)'` are equivalent. In RPL, separate a variable and the operator: `N ?` or `N Termial`. Ordinary RPL identifiers can still contain question marks; use the explicit name prefix `Ⓥ` when quoting such a name inside algebraic syntax. The explicit constant `Ⓒ?` is unchanged.
